course: dictionary
lesson: 14083
title: Mediaeval: a time and a meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mediaeval looks long, but it has clues. Medi means middle, and aeval is about age. Its usual spelling is medieval, and you will see both in books. Historians use it for the Middle Ages, the time in Europe from about 500 to 1500 AD.
explain: «The class visited a mediaeval castle with thick stone walls and a deep moat.» The words castle, walls and moat are clues that this place is from long ago. Mediaeval here means from the Middle Ages, not just old. Check by swapping in your meaning: «from the Middle Ages» still makes sense, and «very old» fits too, but the history meaning is more exact.
explain: People also use mediaeval to complain. «Our head teacher says the new rules are positively mediaeval.» The clues are positively and the rules being harsh. This meaning is informal and negative: very old-fashioned or cruel. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Mediaeval means from or to do with the Middle Ages, about 500 to 1500 AD.
fact: Mediaeval is usually spelled medieval, and you will see both spellings.
fact: «Mediaeval» can also mean very old-fashioned or cruel, as in «mediaeval punishments».
fact: Mediaeval castles, knights and monasteries are studied in history lessons.
fact: Useful phrases: mediaeval times, mediaeval village, mediaeval castle.
exercise: «The class visited a mediaeval castle with thick stone walls.» What does mediaeval mean here? | Painted bright pink | Built last year by a builder | Made of plastic and glass | *From the Middle Ages, about 500 to 1500 AD
exercise: Ella says, «Mum's bedtime rule at six is positively mediaeval.» What does she mean? | Very modern and exciting | *Very old-fashioned and harsh | The same as a bedtime story | A rule about knights and castles
exercise: Which word is another spelling of mediaeval? | median | medal | *medieval | medium
test: «Our class is studying mediaeval times, when knights rode through villages.» What period does mediaeval times mean? | Today's time | *The Middle Ages, about 500 to 1500 AD | The year 2000 | The Stone Age
test: «The punishment for stealing bread was mediaeval, and it was cruel.» What does mediaeval suggest about the punishment? | Kind and gentle | Short and quiet | *Very harsh and old-fashioned | Quick and fun
exam: In «a mediaeval village», what does mediaeval mean? | Full of new shops | Sunny and warm | Very modern | *From the Middle Ages
